.SS "template<uint32_t dim> bool \fBcsmp::Node\fP< dim >::UnitNormal (\fBPoint\fP< dim > & avg_nrml) const"

.PP
for node forming part of line elements (2D) or surface elements (3D), method returns a unit normal that represents the average of the normals of the connected elements If node is part of line elements (2D) or surface elements (3D), method returns a unit normal that represents the average of the normals of the connected elements\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
false if 1) the node is not located on the inside of a patch of lower dimensional elements, 2) not properly initialised or 3) adjacent element normals are pointing in opposite directions 
.RE
.PP

.SS "template<uint32_t dim> uint32_t \fBcsmp::Node\fP< dim >::UpdateNeighbors ()"

.PP
removes null pointers and potential duplicates returning the resulting number of neighbors Sorts vector and removes duplicates and nullptrs\&. The vector is trimmed so that size matches capacity\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBPoint\fP< dim > \fBcsmp::Node\fP< dim >::VertexNormal (typename std::vector< \fBNode\fP< dim > * >::const_iterator first, typename std::vector< \fBNode\fP< dim > * >::const_iterator last) const"

.PP
normal to surface mesh at the \fBNode\fP as based on its connectivity with the surrounding nodes on the surface (cf\&., computer graphics) TODO: fails for quadrilateral meshes Computes normal to \fBNode\fP from its neighbor nodes, but ignoring neighbors that are not contained with the supplied \fBNode\fP vector (as in computer graphics) Supplying this vector allows to narrow the calculation to nodes that lie on a line or surface\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
The method was created to help check the consistency of the node numbering of lower-dimensional elements representing surfaces prior to converting them into boundaries\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfirst\fP iterator to first node in the restricted node range that shall be considered (so that a geometric element can be captured) 
.br
\fIlast\fP iterator to last node in the restricted node range that shall be considered (so that a geometric element can be captured) 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
either the vertex normal or a \fBPoint\fP object initialised with signalling NaN
.RE
.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
std::find() is used so that the supplied \fBNode\fP range does not have to be sorted (or may consist of 2 sorted ranges, like in a model subdomain)
.RE
.PP
Explanation of algorithm: for each vertex, calculate the normal of the plane formed by the two edges entering and leaving that vertex\&. More formally, given vertices 𝐯1,𝐯2,…𝐯𝑛 with counterclockwise winding, define the normal at the 𝑖th vertex as: 
.PP
.nf
 𝐧𝑖=(𝐯𝑖−𝐯𝑖−1)×(𝐯𝑖+1−𝐯𝑖)

.fi
.PP

.PP
(where the indices wrap around)\&. The algorithm is implemented using the MJL library in the discretisation/ directory

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
SKM 
.RE
